Local changes:
- Removed libvgm device-definition glue and framework dependencies; replaced
  simple integer/sample typedefs with standard stdint.h equivalents.
- Replaced left shift of negative LFO sample with multiplication to avoid C UB.
- Increased waveform and LFO phase precision from 12 to 32 fractional bits,
  using 64-bit counters and increments. This prevents distinct hardware
  dividers from collapsing to the same pitch at clock/16 rendering; native
  12-bit frequency registers and noise counters/increments are unchanged.
- adapter.c exports a narrow constructor/destructor/register/single-frame API.

No Ootake code, ROMs, manufacturer waveforms, samples or patch data included.
The LICENSE file expands the source's SPDX BSD-3-Clause designation.
Native model limitations retained from the audited core: LFO frequency has not
been verified against hardware; waveform read/write pointer behavior is not
cycle-accurate. Noise uses the source's deterministic 18-bit LFSR, not rand().
